window.EN={"1":"With Roy and the Lycian alliance army's recapture of the Etrurian royal capital Aquleia as a turning point,","2":"the other Etrurian factions who had been watching and waiting","3":"one after another swung over to the anti-coup faction, and Prime Minister Roartz and Western Isles Governor-General Arcardo's coup faction were driven out of Etruria,","4":"fleeing into the Ilia region, which lay under the power of the kingdom of Bern.","5":"The Ilia region is land spread across the continent's north, with short summers and long winters—amid such harsh nature,","6":"knight orders had been founded in each locale for self-defense, and under their guidance the wastelands had been cleared.","7":"The kingdom of Etruria was liberated. Under King Mordred,","8":"Roy and the others formed a combined army with the Lycian Alliance,","9":"dispatching troops to Ilia to pursue the coup faction,","10":"and at the same time, in order to resolve the root of the problem, decided to also strike at the kingdom of Bern behind it.","11":"Roy, not wishing to stand in the shadow of the Lycian Alliance, and also considering the effect on Etruria's knight orders and the like,","12":"deliberately took to calling it the \"Etrurian army\" and became the commander of the combined force,","13":"and with the cooperation of the Church of Elimine, set out on the expedition.","14":"But what stood before Roy and the others, on top of the harshness of cold Ilia's climate,","15":"was the Bern army commanded by General Murdock, foremost of Bern's Three Dragon Generals who held sway over the Ilia region,","16":"and following him, a portion of Ilia's various knight orders.","17":"In the midst of all this, Roy and the others approach Castle Remy, near the border into Ilia.","18":"Has Narcian... fallen?","19":"Yes... Lord Murdock. Was it truly fine not to help him?","20":"Those are His Majesty's orders.","21":"Besides, a man who can't even clean up the mess he's sown himself has no place in this Bern army.","22":"M-Lord Murdock... whatever will become of us?","23":"Lord Arcardo, I leave this Remy to you. Lord Roartz, I leave Edessa to you.","24":"Each of you see to it. Prepare your counterattack.","25":"Wha—! Hold on just a moment!","26":"Being this close to the Etrurian capital, the enemy will come attack us right away, won't they!","27":"But by that same measure, it'll be easy for us to strike from here too.","28":"Edessa, you say... isn't that deep in Ilia's hinterlands...?","29":"It seems to me a fine place to prepare a counterattack, wouldn't you say?","30":"...W-won't you take back Etruria for us, with Bern's strength?","31":"If we win that way, Etruria becomes Bern's territory—will that still be acceptable to you?","32":"T-that's a problem!","33":"Then you'll just have to manage somehow on your own.","34":"Well then, we'll be taking our leave.","35":".........","36":"...Was that treatment of those men really all right?","37":"It's fine. Each man settles his own affairs—that's Bern's way.","38":"More to the point... what was his name, Roy? The enemy's general?","39":"Yes.","40":"To think the Lycian Alliance we beat down so thoroughly has come to amount to this much.","41":"...If the chance arises, I'd like to cross swords with him once, on the battlefield.","42":"We'll soon be at Etruria's border.","43":"Truly, thank you for everything, Priest Yodel.","44":"Thanks to you and the Church of Elimine, the preparations for the expedition went off without a hitch.","45":"Not at all. If Lord Roy hadn't recaptured the capital Aquleia for us,","46":"we would surely still be under the rule of the kingdom of Bern even now, continuing to suffer under oppression.","47":"When I think of that, this much is nothing at all.","48":"I'm glad to have been of use.","49":"Lord Roy, actually, there's a favor I'd like to ask of you, if I may.","50":"What is it? If it's something I can do...","51":"At the place you're headed from here, if you learn anything new about the \"dragons\"...","52":"I understand. I'll let Priest Yodel know whenever that happens.","53":"I'm grateful! I'll be counting on you.","54":"Oh, and one more thing I must tell you.","55":"About this Remy Bay.","56":"According to the locals, at a certain time of day, a path of sand is said to form across the inlet...","57":"...A path? You mean it becomes possible to cross the sea?","58":"That's right. The castle you can see on the far shore here—","59":"ordinarily, it's a place you could only reach by going quite far around.","60":"But if what they say about the path is true,","61":"wouldn't the march on that Castle Remy become much easier?","62":"I see.","63":"To win in battle, rushing isn't always the quickest way.","64":"Understood. I'll give it some thought.","65":"Well then, may the Etrurian army have the Saint Elimine's blessing!","66":"You lot, are you going to fight against Bern's army?","67":"If so, please, take this staff with you.","68":"They say it's a staff some highborn princess once used, or something like that...","69":"Did you know? At a certain time, a path forms in the middle of the sea.","70":"That path—we locals","71":"call it the \"Sea Road.\"","72":"Rather nice, isn't it?","73":"The sea around here has fierce tides.","74":"Before you get used to it, I failed at it plenty myself.","75":"What with it being so, even if you finally set sail, you can't get out to the open sea.","76":"Lord Arcardo! Ugh—there's... a path, in the sea!","77":"What! What do you mean!","78":"Well... when I asked one of the locals, they said the tide goes out around this hour...","79":"No way, that can't be! You lot didn't know that!","80":"Even if you say so, we aren't from around here, so...","81":"Ngh... what is the meaning of this.","82":"...In any case, don't let the enemy cross that path!!","83":"Lord Roy! A report has just come in!","84":"That a path formed in the sea?","85":"Yes.","86":"Priest Yodel's story was true, it seems.","87":"Hm, I wonder if the enemy knew about this beforehand?","88":"No, it seems there's confusion running through the enemy's ranks.","89":"Well then, let's not miss this chance and press the attack all at once!","90":"※If attacked by Douglas: G-General Douglas!","91":"So you've sided with the enemy after all, damn you!!","92":"※If attacked by another unit: W-why has it come to this!","93":"I... I am... a noble of Etruria.","94":"T-to think I'd fall in a place like this... gwah!...","95":"Lord Arcardo...","96":"Even one who rose as far as Governor-General of Etruria's Western Isles,","97":"in the end, amounts to such a trifling thing.","98":"That's right. Even we ourselves could never have imagined, a year ago, that we'd be standing here like this now.","99":"A person's fate—maybe that's just how it is.","100":"And that must be true of the king of Bern as well, surely...","101":"...Oh, Lord Roy, that thing you're holding in your hand there—whatever is it?","102":"This? This is supposedly the \"Fire Emblem.\"","103":"My word, this little jewel is...","104":"I was entrusted with it by Princess Guinevere.","105":"When she handed it to me... the princess looked terribly pained.","106":"She surely wanted, to the very end, to make King Zephiel reconsider...","107":"Hmm... the bond between brother and sister, is it?","108":"From the outside, I'd always thought it an impossible story.","109":"Why is that?","110":"The one you're up against is King Zephiel of Bern, after all!","111":"He's a man suspected of having even laid hands on his own father, no less.","112":"For him to be moved by family feeling—that's hardly...","113":"Wh-what did you say! His own father?","114":"Oh my, Lord Roy, you didn't know?","115":"Zephiel gained his current throne through the death of Bern's former king,","116":"and as for that former king, since his death was so sudden,","117":"all sorts of dark rumors have been circulating.","118":"One of them being that his own son, the current King Zephiel...","119":"An assassination, that is.","120":"...I wonder if Princess Guinevere knows about that.","121":"It's hardly conceivable that she wouldn't know at all.","122":"........."};
